<title>SWITZERLAND: EU ministers' meeting at telecoms talks delayed.</title>
<headline>EU ministers' meeting at telecoms talks delayed.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Friday meeting  by the European Union General Affairs Council, comprising ministers from member states, to review tabled offers in telecoms talks has been delayed to later in the evening, the EU mission in Geneva said.</p>
<p>The meeting, scheduled for 1600 GMT, has been delayed to 2100 GMT amid doubts among negotiators that an accord could be reached by Saturday's deadline because of the tough U.S. line.</p>
<p>U.S. officials declined to give a detailed assessment of the state of play, but said their team to the World Trade Organisation negotiations insisted better offers were still needed from other countries.</p>
<p>One Western trade envoy said the Americans were playing very hard. &quot;It's beginning to look somewhat doubtful unless something gives somewhere.&quot;</p>
<p>--- Reuters Geneva Newsroom 41-22-733 38 31</p>
